WEBVTT

01:00.390 --> 01:07.230
It is said that 70% of the
human brain's capacity is unused.

01:09.230 --> 01:11.290
It's also thought that...

01:11.870 --> 01:15.060
...the mysterious powers that humans
have are hidden in this part of the brain.

01:17.010 --> 01:21.570
The 70% of the brain that is not used...

01:22.340 --> 01:24.070
...is often called this...

01:24.150 --> 01:29.850
<i>Night Head Genesis</i>

01:45.330 --> 01:46.390
I saw it.

01:46.800 --> 01:48.670
I wasn't able to see it till now.

01:50.340 --> 01:53.170
I was able to see what I have
been looking for for a long time.

01:53.240 --> 01:56.070
The virus hasn't been developed yet.

01:56.880 --> 01:58.250
<i>Providence</i>

01:58.250 --> 02:02.080
<i>Providence
Episode 10</i>

02:02.920 --> 02:06.480
Thank you for waiting.
I am Kanako Kurahashi.

02:06.590 --> 02:07.990
How may I help you?

02:08.060 --> 02:10.460
Apparently you have an
important matter to talk about.

02:10.560 --> 02:12.960
I know this is impolite, but...

02:13.030 --> 02:15.830
...what kind of medicine
are you working on right now?

02:17.530 --> 02:20.930
That's not a question I can
simply answer to an outsider.

02:21.240 --> 02:22.900
Who are you guys?

02:22.970 --> 02:24.100
You're doing...

02:24.170 --> 02:27.470
...an experiment associated with an
activity control medicine for a virus, right?

02:27.910 --> 02:29.040
Am I right?

02:29.780 --> 02:32.440
Do I have a need to answer that?

02:35.580 --> 02:37.480
Just who are you guys...

02:37.550 --> 02:38.850
There was a premonition.

02:39.790 --> 02:41.190
Just what is going on?

02:41.260 --> 02:43.950
I don't understand what
you guys are talking about at all.

02:44.060 --> 02:46.150
Do you believe in
supernatural powers?

02:46.260 --> 02:47.420
Supernatural powers?

02:47.500 --> 02:49.430
Like premonitions and predictions...

02:50.170 --> 02:52.070
Premonitions? Predictions?

02:53.130 --> 02:57.260
If I believed in such things,
I wouldn't have a job like this.

02:57.470 --> 03:01.770
Then why do you think we know
the content of the research?

03:02.010 --> 03:04.440
I don't know. Why is that?

03:05.510 --> 03:08.070
Please stop the research right away.

03:08.650 --> 03:10.170
What are you saying?

03:10.420 --> 03:12.390
There was a reliable premonition.

03:12.490 --> 03:16.360
If you continue with this research,
mankind will go to ruins.

03:20.500 --> 03:21.690
Please believe it.

03:21.760 --> 03:23.420
I want to protect you.

03:24.600 --> 03:25.660
Protect?

03:25.730 --> 03:26.560
Yeah.

03:26.630 --> 03:28.230
This is so stupid...

03:28.540 --> 03:29.470
Wait!

03:30.840 --> 03:32.270
Please leave.

03:34.510 --> 03:35.500
Brother...

03:42.250 --> 03:43.880
Are you Miss Kanako Kurahashi?

03:44.420 --> 03:46.280
Yes, that's me.

03:46.450 --> 03:47.720
Is there something...

03:53.700 --> 03:55.190
S-Stop it!

03:57.100 --> 03:57.830
What's the matter?

03:57.900 --> 03:59.420
That woman is in danger!

03:59.500 --> 03:59.930
What?

04:12.210 --> 04:13.010
What is this...

04:13.080 --> 04:14.550
Hey, are you okay?

04:15.850 --> 04:17.750
It's the person that attacked me.

04:18.090 --> 04:19.080
Are you okay?

04:23.960 --> 04:27.720
Now you know.
You are being targeted.

04:28.330 --> 04:30.320
Stop the research right away.

04:31.970 --> 04:33.160
Miss Kurahashi!

04:33.900 --> 04:34.930
Okay?

04:36.000 --> 04:37.100
Let's go, Naoya!

04:37.470 --> 04:39.060
What happened, Miss Kurahashi?

04:39.140 --> 04:40.610
What happened here?

04:41.780 --> 04:47.080
Even at this moment right now,
humans are getting closer to death.

04:47.520 --> 04:50.280
The black flow has
increased in size again.

04:55.920 --> 04:58.650
I saw another vision of death.

04:59.290 --> 05:01.230
On top of the black gloves...

05:01.600 --> 05:03.760
...a silver snake in the left hand...

05:04.230 --> 05:06.460
...a golden elephant
in the right hand...

05:07.000 --> 05:08.590
Two men...

05:08.940 --> 05:10.870
One of them is tall.

05:11.470 --> 05:13.440
The other one is short.

05:14.640 --> 05:16.870
A death body on the black sofa...

05:17.010 --> 05:18.100
Hey, Mom.

05:18.280 --> 05:20.580
There is no way an elephant
could get on someone's palm.

05:21.450 --> 05:22.610
Little boy...

05:22.950 --> 05:24.580
I'm sorry, sir!

05:25.120 --> 05:26.980
You like airplanes, right?

05:27.060 --> 05:28.150
Yeah, I love them!

05:28.590 --> 05:31.290
When you grow up,
you will become a pilot.

05:31.390 --> 05:32.550
Really, old man?

05:32.630 --> 05:33.560
Hey!

05:33.630 --> 05:37.160
Someday he will put his parents
on the passenger plane and fly.

05:38.000 --> 05:41.800
You have such a good son.
Your mother is so fortunate.

05:41.900 --> 05:44.240
Thank you very much, sir.

05:46.410 --> 05:50.780
Then, the plane you are flying
will fall into the ocean.

05:51.210 --> 05:53.040
There are no survivors.

05:53.110 --> 05:55.080
It's a grand accident.

05:56.950 --> 05:59.920
It's fine. Just don't become a pilot.

05:59.990 --> 06:02.480
No! I'm going to become a pilot!

06:02.990 --> 06:03.920
Idiot!

06:04.360 --> 06:08.590
Mr. Kamiya, if you're saying there is
a future for this boy to become a pilot...

06:08.660 --> 06:12.570
...then that means the downfall
of mankind is past that point, right?

06:12.770 --> 06:15.100
Yes, it most likely is.

06:15.170 --> 06:16.970
When is it, sir?

06:17.170 --> 06:21.470
I don't know for sure,
but maybe another 15 or 20 years.

06:21.710 --> 06:24.510
It could be way past that.

06:24.950 --> 06:26.210
Sir...

06:26.550 --> 06:29.110
The two men you were
speaking of before...

06:29.180 --> 06:32.150
Are they Naoto and Naoya Kirihara?

06:32.220 --> 06:34.280
Who is going to die?

06:41.830 --> 06:44.300
I can't say anything certain yet.

06:44.870 --> 06:49.200
The downfall of mankind can be avoided
with the death of Kanako Kurahashi.

06:51.210 --> 06:52.830
That's right.

07:03.720 --> 07:05.850
Are you okay, Miss Kurahashi?

07:06.550 --> 07:10.220
Maybe it would be better
if you took another 2 or 3 days off.

07:10.320 --> 07:12.920
I'm okay. The injury isn't that severe.

07:12.990 --> 07:14.190
But...

07:14.900 --> 07:15.760
Miss Kurahashi?

07:15.830 --> 07:17.560
The criminal was caught.

07:17.930 --> 07:21.390
I can't leave the data
collection for you alone.

07:22.040 --> 07:25.840
If you continue with this research,
mankind will go to ruins.

07:27.210 --> 07:28.940
An idiotic thing like that couldn't...

07:29.440 --> 07:32.470
But the security organization
here is so insecure.

07:32.550 --> 07:34.070
You think it's okay?

07:34.420 --> 07:38.110
It's the same wherever you are
if your opponent has the intention.

07:38.190 --> 07:40.420
What carefree thing are you saying?

07:40.720 --> 07:42.090
That woman that was caught...

07:42.160 --> 07:45.850
Apparently she is keeping her
mouth shut regarding the motive.

07:45.930 --> 07:50.390
On top of that, the two guys that
came to see you ran away, right?

07:50.730 --> 07:52.930
Those two have
nothing to do with this.

07:53.170 --> 07:55.030
The police were saying that too, right?

07:55.100 --> 07:56.930
The circumstantial
evidence is that way.

07:57.000 --> 07:59.500
And the woman that was caught
said she doesn't know them.

07:59.570 --> 08:02.440
But the woman was
unconscious, right?

08:02.510 --> 08:04.210
It's such a strange story.

08:04.280 --> 08:05.250
Mr. Tadano...

08:05.310 --> 08:05.870
Yes?

08:05.950 --> 08:09.440
Do you believe in
supernatural powers?

08:09.650 --> 08:11.680
Supernatural powers?

08:12.150 --> 08:15.090
It's not something you
believe or don't believe.

08:15.160 --> 08:16.890
It's not a belief.

08:17.160 --> 08:18.990
So you believe it exists?

08:19.060 --> 08:21.890
Did you know that the theory of
relativity's concept of space-time...

08:21.960 --> 08:23.950
...and the world that you surpass...

08:24.030 --> 08:28.490
...in the space-time of meditation
in yoga are very similar?

08:28.840 --> 08:29.600
No.

08:29.670 --> 08:33.370
If you investigate thoroughly
into science, in the end...

08:33.440 --> 08:36.880
...I think you can explain the world
of spirit and supernatural powers.

08:37.250 --> 08:39.010
You have a lot of
understanding, don't you.

08:39.080 --> 08:41.570
But it's not like I have
actually seen it, so...

08:41.650 --> 08:44.850
...I won't be convinced unless
I see it with my own eyes.

08:46.320 --> 08:49.020
Unless I see it with my own eyes...

08:50.190 --> 08:52.420
Miss Kurahashi? Are you okay?

08:52.990 --> 08:55.160
You're most likely still tired.

08:55.800 --> 08:57.130
What about premonitions?

08:57.730 --> 08:58.890
Premonitions?

08:59.370 --> 09:06.270
Nostradamus' premonition of the earth
going to ruins in 1999 was totally off.

09:06.510 --> 09:08.480
A reliable premonition was made...

09:10.280 --> 09:11.070
Stupid...

09:11.150 --> 09:11.870
What?

09:11.950 --> 09:13.240
It's nothing.

09:19.320 --> 09:21.450
Yes. This is Kurahashi Research Lab.

09:21.520 --> 09:24.750
If you stay in a place like that,
you're going to be attacked again.

09:24.830 --> 09:25.850
You are...

09:25.990 --> 09:28.220
Your life is being targeted.

09:28.530 --> 09:31.520
If you don't want to be killed,
leave that place immediately.

09:31.770 --> 09:34.000
Not your house either.
You need to go somewhere safe.

09:34.070 --> 09:35.630
I want to meet with you and talk.

09:35.700 --> 09:37.330
Where are you right now?

09:38.240 --> 09:39.330
Okay.

09:40.810 --> 09:41.900
Miss Kurahashi...

09:42.410 --> 09:45.070
I have urgent business to take care of,
so I'll be out. I'll leave the rest to you.

09:45.150 --> 09:45.980
H-Hold on...

10:04.300 --> 10:05.230
You...

10:07.970 --> 10:09.160
Oh, this...

10:09.370 --> 10:12.830
I bought it at the store downstairs.
It's a thank you gift for saving me.

10:12.910 --> 10:13.870
Please come in.

10:18.850 --> 10:20.140
It's beautiful.

10:20.780 --> 10:23.340
It's my first time getting
something like this.

10:25.250 --> 10:29.420
It's my first time giving
a present like this to a man.

10:31.160 --> 10:34.820
So can I hear the continuation
of what you were talking about?

10:35.700 --> 10:38.100
Do you know a guy
named Tsukasa Kamiya?

10:38.230 --> 10:40.030
No, I don't know him.

10:40.100 --> 10:43.300
He's a dangerous predictor,
but his powers are real.

10:44.040 --> 10:45.900
Naoya and Tsukasa Kamiya...

10:46.110 --> 10:48.630
They both saw the same future.

10:48.710 --> 10:50.470
You can also, um...

10:50.880 --> 10:52.510
...make predictions?

10:54.120 --> 10:57.780
If you continue with the research on the
activity control medicine for the virus...

10:57.850 --> 11:00.950
...because of some action,
a mutation is going to occur.

11:01.020 --> 11:04.860
That's going to make humans
fall into an incurable sickness.

11:04.930 --> 11:06.450
Hold on a second.

11:06.530 --> 11:10.730
If this research goes well, we can
make a specific medicine for AIDS.

11:10.970 --> 11:14.200
So you can't just tell me
to stop with no basis at all.

11:14.270 --> 11:17.260
That's not something
I can do that easily.

11:17.510 --> 11:20.840
This is the only way
to change the future.

11:21.710 --> 11:24.580
In reality, your life is
being targeted, right?

11:25.080 --> 11:28.570
If you keep on going, someone
is going to come to kill you again.

11:29.520 --> 11:31.880
There is no guarantee
that you will survive again.

11:36.220 --> 11:37.420
Is it true?

11:37.560 --> 11:39.460
I can only see it.

11:39.590 --> 11:44.030
To change the tragic future,
you have to make a decision.

11:45.370 --> 11:49.360
To stop my research is like being
given a death penalty sentence.

11:52.070 --> 11:53.940
Please believe us.

11:54.110 --> 11:55.940
Give up the research.

11:58.510 --> 11:59.640
Let me think about it.

11:59.710 --> 12:00.740
Hold on.

12:01.020 --> 12:02.180
There isn't much time.

12:03.020 --> 12:04.110
Let go of me.

12:05.520 --> 12:07.040
Don't go back to your house.

12:07.190 --> 12:09.420
You should secure a safe place.

12:09.490 --> 12:12.690
If I die, the future is
going to be bright, right?

12:12.760 --> 12:15.960
Then you shouldn't worry
about me that much.

12:16.800 --> 12:19.130
If you just stop the research,
that's all that's needed.

12:19.200 --> 12:22.930
If I stop the research,
I have a bleak future.

12:23.800 --> 12:25.970
Even then, it's better to stay alive.

12:33.210 --> 12:34.370
Good-bye...

12:43.560 --> 12:45.860
Honey, you should wake up now.

12:54.440 --> 12:57.270
Honey, you're going
to be late for work.

12:58.770 --> 12:59.800
Work?

13:23.960 --> 13:25.400
Good morning, Honey.

13:26.070 --> 13:27.160
Good morning.

13:28.740 --> 13:31.200
If you don't hurry,
you're going to be late.

13:32.540 --> 13:33.370
Yeah...

13:44.390 --> 13:45.250
Naoya...

13:47.150 --> 13:48.820
Where is Naoya?

13:49.120 --> 13:52.020
It's better to forget about your brother.

13:52.090 --> 13:52.590
What?

13:52.590 --> 13:53.990
What?
You were the one that said it.

13:54.090 --> 13:56.320
Not to talk about that anymore...

13:56.530 --> 13:57.520
Lies.

13:57.600 --> 13:59.100
I would never say such a thing...

13:59.100 --> 13:59.770
I would never say such a thing...
You said it!

13:59.770 --> 14:00.320
You said it!

14:00.470 --> 14:04.630
You always said you wanted to have
a normal life. That's what you said!

14:06.470 --> 14:08.910
Why are you here?

14:13.250 --> 14:14.510
Where is this place?

14:15.180 --> 14:16.510
What happened to Naoya?

14:18.490 --> 14:22.480
This is our home, and you
were the one that said...

14:22.560 --> 14:24.820
...you wanted to forget about Naoya.

14:24.890 --> 14:26.260
That's a lie!

14:28.500 --> 14:30.590
This is terrible!
This tablecloth was expensive.

14:30.970 --> 14:32.520
It's going to leave a stain.

14:32.770 --> 14:33.960
Where is Naoya!

14:34.900 --> 14:39.240
Who knows! What the hell,
your dream life finally came true...

14:39.310 --> 14:41.930
...but now you're all of a sudden
asking about Naoya...

14:42.010 --> 14:42.530
Honey!

14:43.110 --> 14:44.440
Hold on, Honey!

14:44.910 --> 14:45.840
Naoya!

14:45.910 --> 14:47.040
Where are you, Naoya!

14:47.110 --> 14:48.010
Naoya!

15:08.570 --> 15:11.540
Naoya, what's wrong?
Get it together, Naoya!

15:12.410 --> 15:13.460
Naoya!

15:43.470 --> 15:44.770
What're you doing?

15:44.970 --> 15:46.300
You came alone?

15:46.410 --> 15:47.500
That's dangerous.

15:47.740 --> 15:51.200
That's why I came to the safest place.

15:52.550 --> 15:57.380
You said wherever I am it'd be
dangerous, so I got a room in this hotel.

15:59.150 --> 16:01.140
Your brother went to bed?

16:01.460 --> 16:02.180
Yeah...

16:02.260 --> 16:06.060
Do you know what it means
for me to give up on the research?

16:07.060 --> 16:10.590
It's telling me to
throw away part of my life.

16:10.900 --> 16:14.800
If you continue, it means you're
going to abandon your whole life.

16:17.000 --> 16:18.630
What a cold way to say it...

16:18.870 --> 16:19.960
I'm sorry.

16:20.940 --> 16:21.970
Hey...

16:27.850 --> 16:30.080
Why don't we talk in my room?

16:30.450 --> 16:32.750
I can't leave my brother's side.

16:32.920 --> 16:34.180
It's too dangerous.

16:36.460 --> 16:38.720
If you come, I will stop the research.

16:38.790 --> 16:40.560
I'll delete the data too.

16:43.700 --> 16:45.860
I saw a dream earlier.

16:46.330 --> 16:49.170
I shared that dream with you.

16:50.140 --> 16:54.270
I made a stain on one
of your favorite tablecloths.

16:54.640 --> 16:55.800
I'm sorry...

16:57.610 --> 17:00.310
You are a person
with a strong energy.

17:01.050 --> 17:02.140
Yeah...

17:02.820 --> 17:05.110
That's why I can't have a weak man.

17:05.190 --> 17:07.120
They need to be strong like you...

17:09.260 --> 17:11.920
Do you want to try living with me?

17:12.890 --> 17:17.160
You might think it's strange saying
something like this right after we met.

17:18.030 --> 17:23.470
But if I lose my research,
nothing will last for me.

17:24.410 --> 17:27.840
I want another future to replace it with.

17:28.210 --> 17:29.180
Future?

17:29.440 --> 17:30.470
That's right.

17:35.320 --> 17:36.780
Another future...

17:48.060 --> 17:49.150
I can't.

17:50.530 --> 17:51.760
I can't do that.

17:53.630 --> 17:54.570
Really...

18:32.470 --> 18:33.410
Yes.

18:33.810 --> 18:35.540
It's me. You can tell, right?

18:36.310 --> 18:38.280
Yes, is something happening?

18:38.810 --> 18:42.150
I got a phone call from
Kanako Kurahashi before saying...

18:42.220 --> 18:45.880
...she stopped the research
on the virus and deleted the data.

18:45.950 --> 18:47.580
That's a lie.

18:47.860 --> 18:50.420
Okay, that's what Naoya said too.

18:50.490 --> 18:52.460
Does he see it also?

18:52.530 --> 18:54.790
It seems he's been affected by you.

18:54.860 --> 18:56.850
He's slowly becoming able
to see more clearly.

18:57.030 --> 18:59.260
By protecting that woman...

18:59.330 --> 19:03.130
...you are making the
black flow become stronger.

19:03.340 --> 19:07.430
To end the war, we also have
the option of using missiles.

19:08.510 --> 19:10.600
Aren't we suppose to think of a future...

19:10.680 --> 19:13.700
...where the downfall won't come
and Kanako Kurahashi is still alive?

19:14.720 --> 19:16.650
You're whitewashing it.

19:16.720 --> 19:18.620
It's no use talking to you any more.

19:18.690 --> 19:19.810
Hold on.

19:19.950 --> 19:21.850
I have something
I want to ask you too.

19:22.020 --> 19:22.950
What is it?

19:23.260 --> 19:25.850
Silver snake. Golden elephant.

19:26.290 --> 19:27.730
Black gloves.

19:27.960 --> 19:31.160
And now I have seen a new vision.

19:32.100 --> 19:35.800
White powder. The death
of someone on a black sofa.

19:36.370 --> 19:39.900
Do you have any
recognition of these images?

19:39.970 --> 19:40.800
I don't.

19:55.560 --> 19:57.320
White powder...

19:57.690 --> 19:58.720
What is it?

19:59.330 --> 20:00.760
Kamiya said that too.

20:01.130 --> 20:03.690
Black gloves and white powder...

20:08.000 --> 20:12.060
Have you ever thought you wanted
to kill the person that rejected you?

20:17.310 --> 20:18.640
Miss Kurahashi!

20:21.580 --> 20:22.950
What's the matter?

20:23.050 --> 20:25.610
The compounding is weird. Look...

20:28.960 --> 20:30.220
Miss Kurahashi?

20:31.860 --> 20:35.850
I was told to stop the research for
the virus activity control medicine.

20:36.130 --> 20:36.990
By who?

20:37.200 --> 20:40.790
If I continue with the research,
a mutation will occur...

20:40.900 --> 20:43.670
...and that will be the
basis of mankind falling.

20:44.540 --> 20:47.010
The cause is me, apparently.

20:47.370 --> 20:52.740
There was a premonition like that, and
that's why that woman came to kill me.

20:53.010 --> 20:54.500
What the heck is that?

20:54.750 --> 20:56.580
A person that has the
power of precognition...

20:56.650 --> 20:58.950
...told me that he
saw a future like that.

21:00.050 --> 21:01.540
An idiotic thing like that couldn't...

21:05.660 --> 21:09.760
We can come in this easily.
I don't think that the security is perfect.

21:10.300 --> 21:11.790
Do you understand?

21:12.130 --> 21:14.000
What is with you people?

21:14.070 --> 21:15.430
It's okay, Mr. Tadano.

21:15.600 --> 21:16.900
Miss Kurahashi?

21:17.140 --> 21:18.700
They are my visitors.

21:18.910 --> 21:21.030
Please, come in.

21:24.510 --> 21:26.240
Did you stop your research?

21:29.250 --> 21:30.420
Y-You guys are...

21:30.420 --> 21:31.420
Y-You guys are...
Mr. Tadano, go get some drinks.

21:31.420 --> 21:32.680
Mr. Tadano, go get some drinks.

21:32.750 --> 21:33.980
Miss Kurahashi...

21:34.220 --> 21:35.420
Please.

21:49.900 --> 21:50.800
What's happening...

21:56.280 --> 21:58.680
<i>Danger! Due to strong poison,
be careful when handling.</i>

22:06.820 --> 22:09.120
What's the word?
Did you stop the research?

22:09.460 --> 22:11.420
Yes, of course.

22:29.910 --> 22:38.720
<i>I hope that everything that
makes you sad will all disappear.</i>

22:38.790 --> 22:47.560
<i>The words that I said that day
are still tightening my chest.</i>

22:47.630 --> 22:56.400
<i>A single shadow looked like light
in this world that I'm imprisoned in.</i>

22:56.470 --> 23:05.210
<i>The rain of May became lighter
as it was kindly shining tomorrow.</i>

23:05.280 --> 23:09.610
<i>I lost the meaning of smiling...</i>

23:09.680 --> 23:13.980
<i>... that day I thought I
lost my place to be.</i>

23:14.050 --> 23:18.420
<i>I wished for your warmth.</i>

23:18.490 --> 23:22.930
<i>We have stopped time.</i>

23:23.160 --> 23:27.260
<i>I had this feeling it was
eventually going to come, but...</i>

23:27.330 --> 23:31.900
<i>... I pretended I didn't know
and buried my loneliness.</i>

23:31.970 --> 23:42.080
<i>I looked down at your feet as the
droplets describing "Good-bye" fell.</i>

23:42.720 --> 23:51.450
<i>I hope that everything that
makes you sad will all disappear.</i>

23:51.530 --> 23:59.900
<i>The words that I said that day
are still tightening my chest.</i>

24:03.670 --> 24:06.400
The future that was
covered by jet-black darkness...

24:06.940 --> 24:11.780
That was the future of hope
that should have been avoided.

24:12.780 --> 24:14.910
When they get past
the warped thoughts...

24:14.980 --> 24:17.450
...that are dramatized
because of their pureness...

24:17.720 --> 24:21.120
...new dark clouds
creep closer to us.

24:22.190 --> 24:29.900
<i>Episode 11, "Nightmare."</i>

24:25.360 --> 24:28.560
Where are we headed?
